<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project ToolsVersion="15.0" DefaultTargets="Build" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/developer/msbuild/2003">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <VSToolsPath Condition="'$(VSToolsPath)' == ''">$(MSBuildExtensionsPath32)\Microsoft\VisualStudio\v$(VisualStudioVersion)</VSToolsPath>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <Import Project="$(MSBuildExtensionsPath)\$(MSBuildToolsVersion)\Microsoft.Common.props" Condition="Exists('$(MSBuildExtensionsPath)\$(MSBuildToolsVersion)\Microsoft.Common.props')" />
  <PropertyGroup>
    <Configuration Condition=" '$(Configuration)' == '' ">Debug</Configuration>
    <Platform Condition=" '$(Platform)' == '' ">AnyCPU</Platform>
    <SchemaVersion>2.0</SchemaVersion>
    <ProjectTypeGuids>{82b43b9b-a64c-4715-b499-d71e9ca2bd60};{FAE04EC0-301F-11D3-BF4B-00C04F79EFBC}</ProjectTypeGuids>
    <ProjectGuid>{9a6a9e2a-2b0c-4c7f-8f0f-7f7a8d9b6c11}</ProjectGuid>
    <OutputType>Library</OutputType>
    <RootNamespace>Kubuno.VisualStudio</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Kubuno.VisualStudio</AssemblyName>
    <AppDesignerFolder>Properties</AppDesignerFolder>
    <TargetFrameworkVersion>v4.8</TargetFrameworkVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <GeneratePkgDefFile>true</GeneratePkgDefFile>
    <UseCodebase>true</UseCodebase>
    <IncludeAssemblyInVSIXContainer>true</IncludeAssemblyInVSIXContainer>
    <IncludeDebugSymbolsInVSIXContainer>true</IncludeDebugSymbolsInVSIXContainer>
    <IncludeDebugSymbolsInLocalVSIXDeployment>false</IncludeDebugSymbolsInLocalVSIXDeployment>
    <CopyBuildOutputToOutputDirectory>true</CopyBuildOutputToOutputDirectory>
    <CopyOutputSymbolsToOutputDirectory>true</CopyOutputSymbolsToOutputDirectory>
    <StartAction>Program</StartAction>
    <StartProgram Condition="'$(DevEnvDir)' != ''">$(DevEnvDir)devenv.exe</StartProgram>
    <StartArguments>/rootsuffix Exp</StartArguments>
    <MinimumVisualStudioVersion>17.0</MinimumVisualStudioVersion>
    <!--
      Combining several first-party Microsoft.VisualStudio.* NuGet packages of slightly different
      vintages (Microsoft.VisualStudio.SDK 17.14.x pulling 18.x-era transitive VS assemblies vs.
      Microsoft.VisualStudio.Workspace.VSIntegration 17.12.19 and the VS-install-only
      TestWindow/EnvDTE assemblies Kubuno.Rust.TestAdapter/Kubuno.Core.Mcp.Bridge resolve against) makes
      MSBuild's reference unification report an MSB3277 "unresolved conflict" note for each one it
      auto-resolves (always by picking the highest version - the same resolution the running VS
      instance itself performs at load time). This is expected/benign for a VSSDK extension
      referencing this many VS SDK packages at once, not a real version mismatch to fix by hand;
      suppressed here rather than silenced per-conflict, which would need re-editing on every SDK
      package bump.
    -->
    <MSBuildWarningsAsMessages>$(MSBuildWarningsAsMessages);MSB3277</MSBuildWarningsAsMessages>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <PropertyGroup Condition=" '$(Configuration)|$(Platform)' == 'Debug|AnyCPU' ">
    <DebugSymbols>true</DebugSymbols>
    <DebugType>full</DebugType>
    <Optimize>false</Optimize>
    <OutputPath>bin\Debug\</OutputPath>
    <DefineConstants>DEBUG;TRACE</DefineConstants>
    <ErrorReport>prompt</ErrorReport>
    <WarningLevel>4</WarningLevel>
    <DeployExtension>True</DeployExtension>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <PropertyGroup Condition=" '$(Configuration)|$(Platform)' == 'Release|AnyCPU' ">
    <DebugType>pdbonly</DebugType>
    <Optimize>true</Optimize>
    <OutputPath>bin\Release\</OutputPath>
    <DefineConstants>TRACE</DefineConstants>
    <ErrorReport>prompt</ErrorReport>
    <WarningLevel>4</WarningLevel>
    <DeployExtension>False</DeployExtension>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <!--
    The VSIX packaging project and composition root of the extension (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, "Layers (as built)"): the
    package class with every registration attribute (KubunoPackage.cs), the command table (KubunoCommands.vsct), the
    unified settings manifest and its resources, the VSIX manifest - and the layer assemblies, pkgdef fragments,
    grammars, templates, image manifests and bundled tools it ships. No feature code lives here: each layer
    (src/Core, src/Rust, src/Desktop, src/Web, src/Mobile) owns its own.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="PackageGuids.cs" />
    <Compile Include="KubunoPackage.cs" />
    <Compile Include="Properties\AssemblyInfo.cs" />
    <Compile Include="source.extension.cs">
      <AutoGen>True</AutoGen>
      <DesignTime>True</DesignTime>
      <DependentUpon>source.extension.vsixmanifest</DependentUpon>
    </Compile>
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <VSCTCompile Include="KubunoCommands.vsct">
      <ResourceName>Menus.ctmenu</ResourceName>
    </VSCTCompile>
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="source.extension.vsixmanifest">
      <SubType>Designer</SubType>
      <Generator>VsixManifestGenerator</Generator>
      <LastGenOutput>source.extension.cs</LastGenOutput>
    </None>
    <!--
      The display-name resource id [ProvideEditorFactory(typeof(KbviewEditorFactory), 110)] needs (Kubuno.Desktop's
      Designer\INTEGRATION.md section 3) and the key binding table name (#120), resolved through this package's own
      managed resources (PackageRegistration(UseManagedResourcesOnly = true)). ManifestResourceName is set explicitly
      to "VSPackage" (rather than the default namespace-qualified name) because that is the exact base name
      Microsoft.VisualStudio.Shell.Package's own resource lookup expects - the standard VSSDK project template
      convention for this file.
    -->
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Resources\VSPackage.resx">
      <MergeWithCTO>true</MergeWithCTO>
      <ManifestResourceName>VSPackage</ManifestResourceName>
    </EmbeddedResource>
    <!-- Labels and descriptions of the unified settings of every layer (English, and the French satellite); generated
         by tools/gen-unified-settings.ps1, referenced by the manifest as "@Name;..\Kubuno.VisualStudio.dll". -->
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Resources\Settings.resx" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Resources\Settings.fr.resx" />
    <!-- Visual Studio 2026's unified settings page (Tools > Options > Kubuno), registered by KubunoPackage's [ProvideSettingsManifest]. -->
    <Content Include="UnifiedSettings\kubuno.registration.json">
      <IncludeInVSIX>true</IncludeInVSIX>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
    </Content>
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Each layer's static registrations, grammars, image manifests and templates, shipped at the SAME paths inside the
    VSIX as before the layers (pkgdef files at the root, Grammars\, ProjectTemplates\, ItemTemplates\): the files live
    in their layer's folder, only their VSIX path is decided here.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- ==== Rust layer ==== -->
    <!-- rust-analyzer's TextMate grammar and language configuration (Kubuno.Rust\languages.pkgdef). -->
    <Content Include="..\Rust\Kubuno.Rust\languages.pkgdef">
      <IncludeInVSIX>true</IncludeInVSIX>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Link>languages.pkgdef</Link>
    </Content>
    <Content Include="..\Rust\Kubuno.Rust\Grammars\*.*">
      <IncludeInVSIX>true</IncludeInVSIX>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Link>Grammars\%(Filename)%(Extension)</Link>
    </Content>
    <!-- .rsproj project type registration (docs/RSPROJ.md work package 3) - see the file's own header. -->
    <Content Include="..\Rust\Kubuno.Rust.ProjectSystem\rsproj.pkgdef">
      <IncludeInVSIX>true</IncludeInVSIX>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Link>rsproj.pkgdef</Link>
    </Content>
    <!-- .rsproj project node and file icons: discovered by VS's image service from the extension folder; the
         XAML images it references are WPF resources of Kubuno.Rust.ProjectSystem.dll. -->
    <Content Include="..\Rust\Kubuno.Rust.ProjectSystem\Resources\RustProject.imagemanifest">
      <IncludeInVSIX>true</IncludeInVSIX>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Link>RustProject.imagemanifest</Link>
    </Content>
    <!--
      docs/RSPROJ.md Addendum (lot 7): "Create a new project"/"Add New Item" templates. Unlike the
      "Path"-only Asset entries a stock VSIX Project Template item adds by default, this VSSDK
      version's packaging step (Microsoft.VsSDK.targets' CollectVSIXItems) only picks up files it
      already knows about as project items - the two ProjectTemplate/ItemTemplate Asset entries in
      source.extension.vsixmanifest do nothing on their own without these explicit, wildcarded
      Content items (verified live: omitting them produced a .vsix with no template files at all).
      %(RecursiveDir) preserves each template's own subfolder under ProjectTemplates/ItemTemplates.
      Each layer keeps its own templates (Rust: console app, library, module, Rust items; Desktop: desktop
      application, views, controls, components); the VSIX merges them into one catalog.
    -->
    <Content Include="..\Rust\Kubuno.Rust\ProjectTemplates\**\*.*">
      <IncludeInVSIX>true</IncludeInVSIX>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Link>ProjectTemplates\%(RecursiveDir)%(Filename)%(Extension)</Link>
    </Content>
    <Content Include="..\Rust\Kubuno.Rust\ItemTemplates\**\*.*">
      <IncludeInVSIX>true</IncludeInVSIX>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Link>ItemTemplates\%(RecursiveDir)%(Filename)%(Extension)</Link>
    </Content>

    <!-- ==== Desktop layer ==== -->
    <!-- The .kbview grammar, language configuration, core text editor mapping and Open Folder icon
         (Kubuno.Desktop\Views\kbview-languages.pkgdef), the grammar under its own Grammars\Kbview\ subfolder so each
         grammar's THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md/LICENSE files stay unambiguous (different upstream licenses/attribution). -->
    <Content Include="..\Desktop\Kubuno.Desktop\Views\kbview-languages.pkgdef">
      <IncludeInVSIX>true</IncludeInVSIX>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Link>kbview-languages.pkgdef</Link>
    </Content>
    <Content Include="..\Desktop\Kubuno.Desktop\Views\Grammars\*.*">
      <IncludeInVSIX>true</IncludeInVSIX>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Link>Grammars\Kbview\%(Filename)%(Extension)</Link>
    </Content>
    <!-- Kubuno control icons (docs/DESIGNER.md section 11): the designer's Toolbox items and the .kbview element nodes
         of Solution Explorer; the XAML icons are WPF resources of Kubuno.Desktop.ProjectSystem.dll. -->
    <Content Include="..\Desktop\Kubuno.Desktop.ProjectSystem\Resources\KubunoControls.imagemanifest">
      <IncludeInVSIX>true</IncludeInVSIX>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Link>KubunoControls.imagemanifest</Link>
    </Content>
    <Content Include="..\Desktop\Kubuno.Desktop\ProjectTemplates\**\*.*">
      <IncludeInVSIX>true</IncludeInVSIX>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Link>ProjectTemplates\%(RecursiveDir)%(Filename)%(Extension)</Link>
    </Content>
    <Content Include="..\Desktop\Kubuno.Desktop\ItemTemplates\**\*.*">
      <IncludeInVSIX>true</IncludeInVSIX>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Link>ItemTemplates\%(RecursiveDir)%(Filename)%(Extension)</Link>
    </Content>

    <!-- ==== Web and Mobile layers: nothing to ship yet. ==== -->
  </ItemGroup>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <!--
      kubuno-views-ls.exe (Rust LSP server, Kubuno.Desktop.Views' INTEGRATION.md #6) - built
      out-of-band from the separate `desktop` repo
      (Z:\src\desktop\windows, crate kubuno-views-ls):
        cd Z:\src\desktop\windows
        $env:CARGO_TARGET_DIR = "C:\kubuno-build\desktop-target"   # this workspace's documented default (vskubuno/CLAUDE.md #5)
        cargo build -p kubuno-views-ls -r        (-r is cargo's short form of the "release" flag)
      Default matches that convention; override with /p:KubunoViewsLsExePath=<path> for a
      differently-configured CARGO_TARGET_DIR, or in CI (see .github/workflows/build.yml, which
      checks out kubuno/desktop and builds this crate before invoking MSBuild).
    -->
    <KubunoViewsLsExePath Condition="'$(KubunoViewsLsExePath)' == ''">C:\kubuno-build\desktop-target\release\kubuno-views-ls.exe</KubunoViewsLsExePath>
    <!--
      kubuno-views-ls.exe is NOT self-contained: the desktop workspace links kubuno-ui as a Rust
      dylib with -C prefer-dynamic (desktop/windows/.cargo/config.toml), so the exe imports
      kubuno_ui.dll and Rust's own std-<hash>.dll. Shipped alone it dies at load time with
      STATUS_DLL_NOT_FOUND (0xC0000135) before reading a single byte of stdin, which VS reports as a
      JSON-RPC ConnectionLostException during "initialize". Both DLLs are therefore shipped beside it
      in tools\ (the Windows loader looks in the exe's own folder first):
        - kubuno_ui.dll comes from the SAME cargo build as the exe (Cargo uplifts it next to the exe);
          a Rust dylib has no stable ABI, so it must never be mixed with a different build.
        - std-*.dll comes from the toolchain that built the exe (default: the stable MSVC toolchain
          this workspace documents, vskubuno/CLAUDE.md #5); override with /p:KubunoRustStdDir=<dir>.
    -->
    <KubunoViewsLsDir>$([System.IO.Path]::GetDirectoryName('$(KubunoViewsLsExePath)'))\</KubunoViewsLsDir>
    <!--
      kubuno-data-tool.exe (docs/DATA.md DATA-5: the Data Explorer's helper, JSON lines over stdio; crate
      kubuno-data-tool of the desktop repo). Shipped in tools\ BESIDE kubuno-views-ls.exe and sharing its
      tools\kubuno_ui.dll / std-*.dll, so it MUST come from the SAME cargo build (same CARGO_TARGET_DIR, same
      toolchain) as kubuno-views-ls.exe - a Rust dylib has no stable ABI:
        cd Z:\src\desktop\windows
        $env:CARGO_TARGET_DIR = "C:\kubuno-build\desktop-target"
        cargo build -r -p kubuno-views-ls -p kubuno-data-tool
      Override with /p:KubunoDataToolExePath=<path> (then also point KubunoViewsLsExePath at the same build).
    -->
    <KubunoDataToolExePath Condition="'$(KubunoDataToolExePath)' == ''">C:\kubuno-build\desktop-target\release\kubuno-data-tool.exe</KubunoDataToolExePath>
    <KubunoRustStdDir Condition="'$(KubunoRustStdDir)' == ''">$(USERPROFILE)\.rustup\toolchains\stable-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc\lib\rustlib\x86_64-pc-windows-msvc\lib\</KubunoRustStdDir>
    <!--
      kubuno-vs-mcp.exe (Kubuno.Core.Mcp, net8.0 - docs/MCP.md "Integration"). Default: this repo's own
      build output for the same $(Configuration) (a ReferenceOutputAssembly=false ProjectReference
      below drives that build as part of this solution/project build - see its own comment for why
      it is not a normal assembly reference). Override with /p:KubunoMcpOutputDir=<path> to ship a
      self-contained `dotnet publish` output instead.
    -->
    <KubunoMcpOutputDir Condition="'$(KubunoMcpOutputDir)' == ''">$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\Core\Kubuno.Core.Mcp\bin\$(Configuration)\net8.0\</KubunoMcpOutputDir>
    <!--
      kubuno-views-surface.exe (Kubuno.Desktop.Designer's own INTEGRATION.md §6, DSG-7's embedded
      design surface): built out-of-band from the desktop repo, same workspace as kubuno-views-ls but a
      SEPARATE CARGO_TARGET_DIR (this crate is still examples-only, see kubuno-views/examples/view_embed.rs -
      built on its own rather than sharing desktop-target's in-flight build):
        cd Z:\src\desktop\windows
        $env:CARGO_TARGET_DIR = "C:\kubuno-build\agent-dsgint"
        cargo build -r -p kubuno-print -j 1 (the wrapper of kubuno-views' surface with the library components linked - kubuno-data's and kubuno-print's - so views holding data or printing components render before a design build - docs/DATA.md, docs/PRINTING.md; plus the cargo "example" flag, spelled with two dashes,
        naming view_embed - omitted above only because a doubled dash is not valid inside an XML
        comment; see src/Desktop/Kubuno.Desktop/Designer/INTEGRATION.md §6 for the literal command)
      Shipped under its OWN tools\surface\ subfolder (see the Content items below), never merged with
      kubuno-views-ls.exe's own tools\kubuno_ui.dll/std-*.dll: a Rust dylib has no stable ABI, and this
      exe comes from a DIFFERENT CARGO_TARGET_DIR, so it needs its OWN matching kubuno_ui.dll copied
      alongside it, not kubuno-views-ls's.
    -->
    <KubunoViewsSurfaceExePath Condition="'$(KubunoViewsSurfaceExePath)' == ''">C:\kubuno-build\agent-dsgint\release\examples\view_embed.exe</KubunoViewsSurfaceExePath>
    <!--
      An example binary lands in <profile>\examples\ but Cargo still uplifts the workspace's own
      dylib (kubuno_ui.dll) one level up, at the profile root <profile>\ - the same layout
      kubuno-views-ls.exe's own KubunoViewsLsDir relies on for a non-example binary, just one
      directory higher here.
    -->
    <!--
      Independently settable rather than derived from KubunoViewsSurfaceExePath (matching
      KubunoRustStdDir's own precedent above): an example binary lands in <profile>\examples\, but
      Cargo still uplifts the workspace's own dylib (kubuno_ui.dll) one level up, at the profile root
      <profile>\ - override together if KubunoViewsSurfaceExePath is overridden to a differently
      shaped CARGO_TARGET_DIR.
    -->
    <KubunoViewsSurfaceProfileDir Condition="'$(KubunoViewsSurfaceProfileDir)' == ''">C:\kubuno-build\agent-dsgint\release\</KubunoViewsSurfaceProfileDir>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <Target Name="KubunoCheckSurfaceExe" BeforeTargets="Build">
    <Error Condition="!Exists('$(KubunoViewsSurfaceExePath)')"
           Text="kubuno-views-surface.exe (view_embed.exe) not found at '$(KubunoViewsSurfaceExePath)'. Build it: cd Z:\src\desktop\windows ; $env:CARGO_TARGET_DIR='C:\kubuno-build\agent-dsgint' ; cargo build --release --example view_embed -p kubuno-print -j 1 (kubuno-print wraps kubuno-views' surface with the data and printing components linked) -- or pass /p:KubunoViewsSurfaceExePath=&lt;path&gt;." />
    <Error Condition="!Exists('$(KubunoViewsSurfaceProfileDir)kubuno_ui.dll')"
           Text="kubuno_ui.dll not found at '$(KubunoViewsSurfaceProfileDir)' (kubuno-views-surface.exe's own profile root). It must ship with the kubuno_ui.dll of the SAME cargo build (own CARGO_TARGET_DIR, do not reuse kubuno-views-ls's copy)." />
  </Target>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      Link's directory (tools\surface\) is honored by VSIX packaging but its filename is NOT -
      verified live by inspecting the built .vsix's zip contents, the exe ships under its own source
      name regardless (see KubunoViewsSurfaceLocator.cs's own comment on this) - so this is left as
      view_embed.exe rather than renamed, matching what actually ships.
    -->
    <Content Include="$(KubunoViewsSurfaceExePath)">
      <IncludeInVSIX>true</IncludeInVSIX>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Link>tools\surface\view_embed.exe</Link>
    </Content>
    <Content Include="$(KubunoViewsSurfaceProfileDir)kubuno_ui.dll" Condition="Exists('$(KubunoViewsSurfaceProfileDir)kubuno_ui.dll')">
      <IncludeInVSIX>true</IncludeInVSIX>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Link>tools\surface\kubuno_ui.dll</Link>
    </Content>
    <KubunoViewsSurfaceStdDll Include="$(KubunoRustStdDir)std-*.dll" />
    <Content Include="@(KubunoViewsSurfaceStdDll)">
      <IncludeInVSIX>true</IncludeInVSIX>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Link>tools\surface\%(Filename)%(Extension)</Link>
    </Content>
  </ItemGroup>

  <Target Name="KubunoCheckToolExes" BeforeTargets="Build">
    <Error Condition="!Exists('$(KubunoViewsLsExePath)')"
           Text="kubuno-views-ls.exe not found at '$(KubunoViewsLsExePath)'. Build it from the desktop repo: cd Z:\src\desktop\windows ; $env:CARGO_TARGET_DIR='C:\kubuno-build\desktop-target' ; cargo build --release -p kubuno-views-ls -- or pass /p:KubunoViewsLsExePath=&lt;path to kubuno-views-ls.exe&gt;." />
    <Error Condition="!Exists('$(KubunoViewsLsDir)kubuno_ui.dll')"
           Text="kubuno_ui.dll not found beside kubuno-views-ls.exe in '$(KubunoViewsLsDir)'. kubuno-views-ls.exe imports it (kubuno-ui is a Rust dylib) and must ship with the kubuno_ui.dll of the same cargo build." />
    <Error Condition="'@(KubunoRustStdDll)' == ''"
           Text="Rust's std-*.dll not found in '$(KubunoRustStdDir)'. kubuno-views-ls.exe imports it (-C prefer-dynamic); pass /p:KubunoRustStdDir=&lt;rustc --print sysroot&gt;\lib\rustlib\x86_64-pc-windows-msvc\lib\ for the toolchain that built it." />
    <Error Condition="!Exists('$(KubunoDataToolExePath)')"
           Text="kubuno-data-tool.exe not found at '$(KubunoDataToolExePath)'. Build it from the desktop repo in the SAME cargo build as kubuno-views-ls.exe (they share tools\kubuno_ui.dll): cd Z:\src\desktop\windows ; $env:CARGO_TARGET_DIR='C:\kubuno-build\desktop-target' ; cargo build --release -p kubuno-views-ls -p kubuno-data-tool -- or pass /p:KubunoDataToolExePath=&lt;path to kubuno-data-tool.exe&gt;." />
  </Target>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Content Include="$(KubunoViewsLsExePath)">
      <IncludeInVSIX>true</IncludeInVSIX>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Link>tools\kubuno-views-ls.exe</Link>
    </Content>
    <!-- docs/DATA.md DATA-5: the Data Explorer's helper, using the tools\kubuno_ui.dll / std-*.dll below (same cargo build, see KubunoDataToolExePath). -->
    <Content Include="$(KubunoDataToolExePath)" Condition="Exists('$(KubunoDataToolExePath)')">
      <IncludeInVSIX>true</IncludeInVSIX>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Link>tools\kubuno-data-tool.exe</Link>
    </Content>
    <!-- kubuno-views-ls.exe's runtime DLLs - see KubunoViewsLsDir/KubunoRustStdDir above. -->
    <KubunoRustStdDll Include="$(KubunoRustStdDir)std-*.dll" />
    <Content Include="$(KubunoViewsLsDir)kubuno_ui.dll" Condition="Exists('$(KubunoViewsLsDir)kubuno_ui.dll')">
      <IncludeInVSIX>true</IncludeInVSIX>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Link>tools\kubuno_ui.dll</Link>
    </Content>
    <Content Include="@(KubunoRustStdDll)">
      <IncludeInVSIX>true</IncludeInVSIX>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Link>tools\%(Filename)%(Extension)</Link>
    </Content>
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    kubuno-vs-mcp.exe's own Content item CANNOT be a plain top-level <ItemGroup> glob like the ones
    above: those are fine because their source files (kubuno-views-ls.exe, view_embed.exe) are built
    OUTSIDE this solution, before this project is even opened, so they already exist on disk the
    moment MSBuild evaluates this file's items - which happens once, during the static EVALUATION
    pass, before any target (including this project's own ProjectReference-driven build of
    Kubuno.Core.Mcp) executes. kubuno-vs-mcp.exe, by contrast, is built AS PART of this same solution
    build (the ReferenceOutputAssembly=false ProjectReference below) - on a clean checkout, nothing
    has built it yet at evaluation time, so a static `Content Include="$(KubunoMcpOutputDir)**\*.*"`
    silently matches ZERO files and the VSIX ships without the MCP bridge, with no error (found live:
    a full clean build produced a Kubuno.VisualStudio.vsix missing tools\kubuno-vs-mcp\ entirely,
    despite 0 build errors/warnings - KubunoCheckToolExes's own Error above never caught it either,
    since by the time THAT target ran - BeforeTargets="Build" - Kubuno.Core.Mcp had, by then, already been
    built by ResolveProjectReferences, so the exists-check passed; only the item glob's own timing
    was wrong). Fixed by moving the glob into a target - AfterTargets="ResolveProjectReferences" ONLY,
    deliberately WITHOUT also pinning it BeforeTargets="Build": found live, by comparing MSBuild
    diagnostic-verbosity target IDs, that combining the two pins a target right before the outer
    "Build" target's own (near-empty) body, which for this VSSDK project only starts after its own
    huge DependsOn chain - including VSSDK's GetVsixSourceItems (the target that actually snapshots
    @(Content) with IncludeInVSIX=true for packaging) and CreateVsixContainer - has ALREADY run; a
    target pinned that way is always too late to contribute Content items, no matter how it is
    triggered. AfterTargets alone inserts right after ResolveProjectReferences's own, much earlier,
    invocation (confirmed live: target id ~46 of ~1750, versus GetVsixSourceItems at id ~1711) - the
    same target that actually builds a ReferenceOutputAssembly=false ProjectReference via its own
    <MSBuild> task, so items are created dynamically at EXECUTION time, once the exe is guaranteed to
    be on disk, well before GetVsixSourceItems collects them - not matched once at evaluation time
    (too early, exe does not exist yet) and not added too late either (past GetVsixSourceItems).
    Verified live end to end: a genuinely clean `msbuild Kubuno.VisualStudio.sln -t:Restore` then
    `-t:Build` (no manual pre-build of Kubuno.Core.Mcp.csproj) produced a Kubuno.VisualStudio.vsix whose
    tools\kubuno-vs-mcp\ contains kubuno-vs-mcp.exe and its full dependency closure. Every file
    Kubuno.Core.Mcp's own build produces (kubuno-vs-mcp.exe/.dll/.deps.json/.runtimeconfig.json and its
    dependency DLLs, e.g. ModelContextProtocol*.dll) - it is a framework-dependent net8.0 exe, not
